  (subsection function-editor
   (doc "Load, edit, and save a binding's AST from the UI")
   (status partial)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "POST /edit/editor-greet save -> callable via /api/eval")
    (smoke "GET /edit/missing-fn shows create affordance, not silent TODO only")
    (smoke "GET /edit/hello after hello-recipe: offers Edit hi-page + Create hello")
    (smoke "htmx POST create missing fn returns editor partial; save works"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         URL: /edit/<function-name>  (function name, NEVER a route path
         as the object of edit — routes are pages).

         v1 SHIPPED: plain textarea editor + save on current branch
         when the binding already exists.

         REQUIRED NEXT — missing binding empty state:
         When GET /edit/<name> and no function_defs row for name:

         1. Do NOT present only a raw TODO stub as if the user is
            already editing a real function.

         2. Show an explicit card:
              Function "<name>" does not exist.

         3. Route awareness: if a page route "/<name>" (or path
            equal to name) exists with handler H:
              There is a page /<name> that currently runs function H.
              Primary:  [ Edit H ]  -> /edit/H
              Secondary:[ Create function <name> ]
              Optional: [ Create <name> and point /<name> at it ]
                (define + route update; power move)
            If no such route: only Create (and link back to Functions).

         4. Create-in-place via htmx (no full-page dead end):
              POST /api/edit/create  {name}  (and optional rebind_route)
              -> 200 HTML partial: the editor form for the new binding
                 (same fields as GET /edit/<name> after create)
              hx-target=#editor-root hx-swap=innerHTML
              Default body stub:
                (lambda ()\n  "TODO: implement <name>")
              After create, user saves via existing POST /edit/<name>.

         5. Creating a function does not silently rename routes unless
            the user chose "point page at it".

         6. Namespaced names (image.packages):
            - Accept full names with `/` (todo/list) in name field.
            - Create form MAY split package + local name and join with `/`.
            - URL routing for /edit/todo/list: either path segments after
              /edit/ joined back to todo/list, or /edit?name=todo%2Flist.
              Prefer path join if http router is easy; document choice.

         DEFERRED: optimistic concurrency / stale-body reject.
         The structural AST tree-editor now lives in
         structural-editing.ast-structure-view (paths first; stable
         node storage still via branching.ast-nodes).
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection inspector
   (doc "Inspect values, rows, ASTs, and page→function graphs live")
   (status partial)
   (implements image/lib/http_pages.ml image/lib/session.ml image/lib/agent_tools.ml)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "GET /inspect/binding/<name> shows author + AST")
    (smoke "GET /page/hello after recipe: handler hi-page listed")
    (smoke "page inspector lists callees of handler when body calls other fns")
    (smoke "(callees \"ui/nav\") returns list; (callers \"ui/menu\") non-empty when nav calls menu")
    (smoke "after redefine of a callee, impact-queue lists dependents + routes")
    (smoke "agent install_function result text names impact routes to smoke"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         ==========================================================
         SHIPPED (v1 inspector)
         ==========================================================
         - binding AST pretty+JSON; data row JSON pretty
         - GET /page/<path>: routing panel + STATIC callee graph
           (App heads that are Vars → visible function_defs;
            depth cap 8; cycles skipped)
         - /bindings "used by": DIRECT handler→route only
           (not full transitive reverse graph — perf; deep graph
            stays on /page inspect). Implementation note 2026-07:
           used_by_pages_map is handler-only to avoid N*depth PG
           lookups on every /bindings load.

         ==========================================================
         CHANGE IMPACT (planned) — reverse deps → test obligations
         ==========================================================
         Motivation (language + OS):
           Live define/install is not proof the habitat still works.
           We already pay for a static call graph on inspect. Use it
           like Smalltalk senders + Nx "affected": when F changes,
           flag who depends on F and which routes to re-smoke.

         Industry analogues (do not overbuild):
           IDE Find References, Bazel/Nx affected, Smalltalk senders,
           coverage-guided test selection. We want the live-image
           version, not a full CI product.

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         A. STATIC GRAPH API (shared kernel)
         ----------------------------------------------------------
         Reuse collect_var_apps / page_function_graph style analysis.

         Forward (already):
           callees(name) → user functions F statically calls
             (direct App Var heads that resolve to function_defs;
              optional ~depth default 1 for prims, 8 for inspect)

         Reverse (NEW — function→function, not only routes):
           Build once per request or cache short-TTL on branch:
             for each visible binding B with body expr:
               for each direct callee C in collect_var_apps(body):
                 callers[C] := callers[C] ∪ {B}
           callers(name) → list of B that directly App-call name
           dependents(name, ~depth) → BFS reverse edges, cap depth
             (default 8), cycle-safe; exclude name itself

         Routes (extend used_by):
           used_by_routes(name):
             - always include routes whose handler = name
             - PLUS routes whose handler's transitive callees
               include name (reuse page_function_graph or reverse
               map from cached forward graphs). Cap cost: compute
               reverse route index when building callers map once
               per branch snapshot, not per /bindings row naively.

         Nopales prims (session-aware, read-only, any authed user):
           (callees name [depth])     → VList of VStr names
           (callers name)             → VList of VStr names (direct)
           (dependents name [depth])  → VList of VStr names
           (used-by-routes name)      → VList of route path strings

         Missing name → () or empty list (not error).
         Prims/kernel names: callers may be empty; still OK.
         IMPORTANT (image.dnu-stubs): callers(name) MUST work when
         name is not yet a function_def — reverse index is built
         from all visible bodies' App-Var heads, not only defined
         callees. holes(name) lives in dnu-stubs; shares walk.

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         B. IMPACT QUEUE (on define / install)
         ----------------------------------------------------------
         When a binding is successfully defined or install_function
         succeeds for NAME on the current branch:

           impact = {
             name: NAME
             at: timestamp
             branch: current branch ref
             author: whoami
             dependents: dependents(NAME)
             routes: used-by-routes(NAME)
             status: pending | smoked | dismissed
           }

         Storage (v1):
           Session-local ring buffer (last N=32 impacts) on Session.t
           is enough for agent + UI banner. Optional later: data_rows
           type impact-event for cross-request durability.

         Surfaces:
           1) Nopales:
                (impact-queue) → list of impact dicts/JSON strings
                (impact-clear [name|all])
                (impact-mark name 'smoked|'dismissed)
           2) define / install_function return path (agent tools):
                append human-readable block:
                  "impact: dependents=…; smoke routes: /a /b"
                If routes empty: "impact: no routes; eval dependents
                  or smoke parents manually"
           3) UI (light):
                /bindings or /edit/<name>: badge "N dependents" +
                link to impact panel; optional site chrome banner
                when queue has pending items for this branch
                (do not block editing).

         Do NOT fail define because dependents exist — only notify.

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         C. "NEEDS TESTING" LADDER
         ----------------------------------------------------------
         L0 (MVP — ship first): awareness only (queue + agent text)
         L1: optional auto eval of pure dependents (if effect pure)
         L2: recommend/auto smoke_route for each used-by-routes entry
             (agent definition-of-done already requires smoke; impact
              tells WHICH paths)
         L3 (later): hard badge red until smoke or dismiss

         Default ship L0+L2-hints. No blocking L3 in v1.

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         D. AGENT SEED
         ----------------------------------------------------------
         After install_function / eval define of a package function:
           - Read impact (tool result or (impact-queue))
           - smoke_route every listed route (GET, contains marker)
           - eval_expr key pure dependents if no routes
           - Final summary must mention impact smokes

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         E. LIMITS (honest static analysis)
         ----------------------------------------------------------
           - No dynamic apply / computed names
           - Higher-order (map f xs) may miss f unless App head
           - Macros: graph is source App Vars (post-expand ideal
             later; v1 source walk matches today's inspector)
           - False negatives possible — route smokes remain truth
           - Noise control: only enqueue when NAME is a stored
             function_def (not every let-bound local); skip if
             dependents and routes both empty

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         F. NON-GOALS
         ----------------------------------------------------------
           - Runtime request traces / dynamic call sampling
           - Full CI product / GitHub integration
           - Coverage-guided line maps
           - Blocking save on dirty dependents
           - Cross-branch impact (only current branch visibility)

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         G. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES
         ----------------------------------------------------------
         Phase I1: shared graph helpers + (callees)/(callers)/
                   (dependents)/(used-by-routes); unit/smoke
                   (callers works for missing names — DNU)
         Phase I2: impact-queue on define + install_function text;
                   (impact-queue)/(impact-clear)/(impact-mark);
                   same hook appends change-transcript
                   (branching.change-set)
         Phase I3: /bindings detail Callers/Callees/Impact badge;
                   agent seed paragraph
         Phase I4 (optional): short-TTL cache; L1 pure auto-eval

         Combo-pack build order (whole five):
           I1 graph → I2 define hooks (impact+changeset) →
           browser detail panels → dnu-stubs → desktop 3-pane

         ----------------------------------------------------------
         H. SUCCESS
         ----------------------------------------------------------
           - Changing ui/menu shows ui/nav (or similar) in callers
           - used-by-routes for a shared helper lists real pages
           - Agent after install is told which routes to smoke
           - /bindings stays fast (no per-row depth-8 walk regress)

         DEFERRED (still): eval-result inspect, type-def deep
         inspect, runtime traces, mutate-from-inspector.

         ==========================================================
         COMBO-PACK NOTE
         ==========================================================
         Inspector owns graph + impact + value inspect (#1, #3).
         Browser hub: image.system-browser. Change transcript:
         branching.change-set. Holes: image.dnu-stubs. Define hook
         is the shared write path for impact + change-set append.
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection dnu-stubs
   (doc "doesNotUnderstand-style holes: unbound names → stub + callers for agents")
   (status planned)
   (implements image/lib/http_pages.ml image/lib/session.ml image/lib/http.ml)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "eval unbound foo yields structured unbound_var with name=foo")
    (smoke "(holes \"ui/nav\") lists App-Var names in body not bound as fn/prim")
    (smoke "POST stub create missing name → callable lambda TODO stub")
    (smoke "unbound route handler page offers Create stub + Callers")
    (smoke "agent after unbound error can stub then see callers of stub name"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         ==========================================================
         WHY (Smalltalk doesNotUnderstand, agent-friendly)
         ==========================================================
         Live images fill holes instead of failing closed forever.
         Agents hit unbound names constantly (typos, planned fns,
         half-migrated packages). Today: bare Unbound_var / handler
         unbound cards. Goal: a closed loop without becoming CI:

           missing name
             → structured error (kind + name)
             → who already calls it? (static callers — may be empty)
             → one-click / one-tool stub (lambda TODO)
             → edit + impact/smoke via existing inspector paths

         This is NOT a full condition system (see
         lisp-interpreter.errors-and-locations for guard/catch).
         DNU here = product UX + agent affordance on holes.

         ==========================================================
         A. STRUCTURED UNBOUND (host)
         ==========================================================
         Keep raising Interp_error (Unbound_var name). Surfaces must
         expose machine fields (align with errors-and-locations C):
           kind: unbound_var
           name: <missing>
           source: optional define/handler context
         /api/eval JSON and agent tool errors include name= so agents
         do not regex the message. REPL print may stay one-line.

         ==========================================================
         B. STATIC HOLES IN A BODY
         ==========================================================
         holes(name) — for stored function NAME:
           walk body with collect_var_apps (same as graph)
           candidate = App-Var heads
           hole if not in: prim registry ∪ visible function_defs
                           ∪ special forms ∪ lambda params / lets
                           (best-effort; App heads only; accept
                            false negatives on dynamic names)
         Nopales: (holes name) → VList of VStr
         UI: browser detail + editor show Holes list.

         ==========================================================
         C. STUB CREATE
         ==========================================================
         Default stub body (same spirit as function-editor missing):
           (lambda ()
             "TODO: implement <name>")
         Zero-arg v1; agent/human edits signature. Never invent args.

         Paths:
           1) function-editor missing card [Create] — already
              specified; dnu-stubs REUSES it (POST /api/edit/create)
           2) Nopales (stub-function name) → define stub if missing;
              error if already bound (use install/edit to overwrite)
           3) Unbound handler HTTP response: card with
                handler H unbound
                [Create stub H] [Edit if exists] [Callers of H]
           4) Agent tool optional stub_function name= — thin wrap
              over same define_binding; seed text: on unbound_var,
              stub → install real body → smoke impact routes

         Creating a stub is a normal define: fires impact-queue +
         change-set transcript hooks.

         ==========================================================
         D. CALLERS OF A HOLE
         ==========================================================
         Even when NAME is unbound, reverse graph still finds B
         whose body App-calls NAME (static). (callers name) must
         work for missing names (build from all visible bodies),
         not only defined callees. Critical for "who wanted this?"

         ==========================================================
         E. NON-GOALS
         ==========================================================
           - Runtime doesNotUnderstand method dispatch / prototype OO
           - Auto-generating real implementations via LLM on every miss
           - Catching unbound inside every page without guard (that's
             errors-and-locations phase 2)
           - Stubbing kernel prim names

         ==========================================================
         F. PHASES
         ==========================================================
         D1: structured unbound name in /api/eval + (holes)
         D2: callers works for missing names; UI holes on detail
         D3: stub-function + unbound handler card + agent note
         D4: wire browser detail Holes panel (system-browser)

         SUCCESS: agent sees unbound: foo with name field, stubs
         foo, finds callers, fills body, impact lists routes.
    |))
   )
  )
 )

)
